      FACTION COMMANDS — GENERAL
      /factions create <faction name> (Create faction)
      /factions join <faction name> (Join a faction)
      /factions leave (Leave a faction)
      /factions disband (Disband your faction)

      FACTION COMMANDS — INFO
      /factions invite add <player name> (Invite player to faction)
      /factions info <faction> (Displays your/another faction's description, members and power levels)
      /factions settings chat (Changes which chat you're currently sending and receiving from)

      FACTION COMMANDS — CLAIMING
      /factions claim add <size> (Claims the chunk you're standing in, or a radius around it.)
      /factions claim remove <size>

      FACTION COMMANDS — SETTINGS
      /f modify open <true|false> (Set your faction to public or invite only)
      /f modify description <faction description>
      /f modify color <color>
      /f modify motd <motd> (Set your faction Message of the Day)
      /f modify name <name>
      /f declare ally <faction name>
      /f declare neutral <faction name>
      /f declare enemy <faction name>

      FACTION COMMANDS — PERMISSIONS
      By default only faction members can interact/place/break blocks in your faction claim. Faction leaders can tweak these settings to provide apartments for members/guests.
      /f permissions faction <faction name> add/remove <permission name>
      /f permissions guest add/remove <permission name>
      /f block blacklist add (blacklist blocks members/guests can't break — useful for apartment walls/floors/ceilings)
      Faction dimension tool available at Lena (create regions where members/guests can't break)

      FACTIONS UPDATE — PLAYER POWER & ACTIVITY
      Each member contributes up to 20 power (by default) to the faction based on activity.
      Inactive players contribute less power over time: 7+ days = 75% power, 14+ days = 50% power, 30+ days = 0% power.
      Power contribution resets when you log in. Check individual power in /f info.

      FACTIONS UPDATE — WEALTH POWER & BANK
      /f sacrifice — deposit valuable items (diamonds, netherite, etc) into the faction bank ($) for wealth power
      Wealth decays daily, and decays faster the richer you are
      /f wealth — view wealth power, bank balance, decay info
      /f wealth add <amount> / withdraw <amount> — convert between bank $ and wealth power (leaders only)
      /f bank / /f bank withdraw <amount> — view/withdraw faction bank balance (leaders only)
      Tip: spend wealth on God's Blessings before it decays away

      FACTIONS UPDATE — WAR POWER
      Earn power by killing players from other factions (2x for enemy faction members)
      War power decays over time if the faction stops fighting. Max 100 by default.

      FACTIONS UPDATE — FAME POWER
      Earned through special activities like dungeons and events. Decays over time. Max 100 by default.

      FACTIONS UPDATE — CLAIM DECAY
      Each claim requires 5 power (by default) to maintain. If faction power drops too low, claims are auto-removed (farthest from faction home first). Check "Required Power" in /f info.

      FACTIONS UPDATE — VASSALS & OVERLORDS
      Factions can offer to become another faction's vassal (must be mutual allies, target faction leader must accept). Overlords gain 25% of vassal's power.
      /f vassal info | offer <faction> | accept <faction> | release <faction> | leave
      Only one level of hierarchy. Overlords can't become vassals. If an overlord disbands, vassals are auto-released.

      FACTIONS UPDATE — GOD'S BLESSINGS
      Leaders use /f gods pray <godname> to grant a potion effect to all online faction members, spending wealth power. Up to 2 blessings active at once. 5 minute cooldown between prayers. Blessings persist through death.
      /f gods — list all gods and costs
      Default gods: Ares (Strength, 5min, cost 25), Athena (Resistance, 5min, cost 30), Hermes (Speed II, 5min, cost 20), Apollo (Regeneration, 3min, cost 35), Hephaestus (Haste II, 5min, cost 15)

      FACTIONS UPDATE — POWER BREAKDOWN
      Total power in /f info comes from: Base, Player, Wealth, War, Fame, Vassal (if overlord), Admin, and Bank ($).

      --- SERVER GUIDE END ---

# Intention Checker - determines when AI should respond
# 意图检查器 - 决定AI何时应该响应
# 意図チェッカー - AIがいつ応答すべきかを決定
intention:

  # Enable intention checking to filter when AI should respond
  # 启用意图检查以过滤AI何时应该响应
  # AIがいつ応答すべきかをフィルタリングする意図チェックを有効化
  enabled: true

  # Use fast path for intention checking (skips some checks for speed)
  # 使用快速路径进行意图检查 (跳过部分检查以提高速度)
  # 意図チェックに高速パスを使用 (速度向上のため一部のチェックをスキップ)
  useFastPath: false

  # Minimum probability threshold for AI to respond (0.0-1.0)
  # AI响应的最小概率阈值 (0.0-1.0)
  # AIが応答する最小確率閾値 (0.0-1.0)
  responseProbabilityThreshold: 0.5

  # Number of recent messages to include in context for intention checking
  # 意图检查时包含的最近消息数量
  # 意図チェックのコンテキストに含める最近のメッセージ数
  contextLength: 10

  # API key for intention checker (leave empty to use main OpenAI key)
  # 意图检查器的API密钥 (留空则使用主OpenAI密钥)
  # 意図チェッカー用のAPIキー (空白の場合はメインのOpenAIキーを使用)
  apiKey: ''

  # Base URL for intention checker API (leave empty to use main URL)
  # IMPORTANT: Must include /v1 path if using OpenAI-compatible API
  # 意图检查器的API基础URL (留空则使用主URL)
  # 重要: 如使用OpenAI兼容API，必须包含 /v1 路径
  # 意図チェッカーAPIのベースURL (空白の場合はメインURLを使用)
  # 重要: OpenAI互換APIを使用する場合は /v1 パスを含める必要があります
  baseUrl: ''

  # Model for intention checking (usually a faster/cheaper model)
  # Personal recommendation: qwen3-235b-a22b-2507 via Cerebras
  # 用于意图检查的模型 (通常使用更快/更便宜的模型)
  # 个人推荐: 通过 Cerebras 使用 qwen3-235b-a22b-2507
  # 意図チェック用のモデル (通常はより高速/安価なモデル)
  # 個人的な推奨: Cerebras経由でqwen3-235b-a22b-2507
  model: nemotron-3-ultra-free

  # Prompts for intention checking system
  # 意图检查系统的提示词
  # 意図チェックシステムのプロンプト
  prompts:

    # System message for intention checker to determine if AI should respond
    # 意图检查器的系统消息，用于确定AI是否应该响应
    # AIが応答すべきかを判断する意図チェッカーのシステムメッセージ
    systemMessage: |-
      You are an AI assistant for a Minecraft server. Analyze the message content and decide if a response is needed.

      Must respond:
      - Direct commands starting with ':' or ':'
      - Explicitly mentioning my name (Joi)
      - Direct questions to me
      - Requests to execute server commands
      Can respond:
      - Players needing help or confused (not when theyre discussing with each other)
      - Important achievements or milestones worth celebrating
      - Players needing comfort
      - When my response makes the conversation more interesting
      - Normal join events (if player join repeatedly dont greet them repeatedly)

      Do not respond:
      - Normal conversations between players
      - Routine game activities (mining/building/trading)
      - Discussions unrelated to me
      - Repetitive or meaningless messages
      - Normal leave events

      Default principle: When in doubt, do not respond.

# Bot behavior and personality settings
# 机器人行为和个性设置
# ボットの動作とパーソナリティ設定
bot:

  # Color code for bot chat (without §). Examples: b=aqua, e=yellow, a=green, c=red
  # 机器人聊天颜色代码 (不含§)。例如: b=青色, e=黄色, a=绿色, c=红色
  # ボットチャットのカラーコード (§なし)。例: b=水色, e=黄色, a=緑, c=赤
